# The append-only state CSVs get git's UNION merge driver.
#
# WHY. Every one of these files is written by EOF append, and two writers append
# different rows to the same last line — a Mac booster and a cloud runner, or two
# runners either side of a queued schedule. The default merge driver reports that
# as a conflict on every single occasion, and an Actions runner has no human to
# resolve it: the commit-back retry aborts the rebase, retries, conflicts
# identically, and after three attempts throws away the whole session INCLUDING
# the ledger rows for evaluations that actually happened. "Every genome evaluation
# of any fidelity appends to the trial ledger" is a constraint of this project, so
# a merge policy that can silently drop those rows is not acceptable.
#
# Union keeps BOTH sides' lines, which for an append-only log is the correct
# resolution and not a compromise.
#
# THE COST, AND WHO PAYS IT. Union can leave the same line twice when both sides
# appended byte-identical rows. For the trial ledger that is always a merge
# artifact — its writer is idempotent on (generation, genome_hash, fidelity), so
# two identical rows can never be two real evaluations — and run_generation and
# run_deepeval dedup it at startup, loudly. The other three files are NOT deduped
# on purpose: two identical vault_access rows are two real looks at the vault,
# two identical deepeval_history rows are two real runs, and collapsing either
# would make a DSR optimistic, which is the one direction this project is not
# allowed to be wrong in. Over-counting is the safe side of that trade.
state/*.csv merge=union

# The returns matrices and artifacts are binary and content-addressed; a conflict
# on one is a real disagreement about content and must not be auto-resolved.
state/returns/*.npz -merge -diff
artifacts/**/*.gz   -merge -diff
